{
  "note": "Synthetic recordings for specs/lora.md. Each frame was modulated as a LoRa (or AFSK) frame, placed at the stated offset with the stated carrier offset, added to complex white Gaussian noise (power 0.002 per sample), and decoded back by an independent demodulator before release. 'snr_db' is the SNR in the LoRa bandwidth that was set; 'cfo_hz' is the carrier offset of the frame from the nominal channel centre. 'start_s' is the first sample of the preamble (seconds from the first sample). Payloads are hex, first byte sent first. Times and payloads are exact; tolerances are in 'tolerance'.",
  "tolerance": {
    "payload_hex": "exact",
    "decoded_fields": "exact (strings, numbers, flags)",
    "start_s": "within one symbol time of the setting",
    "cfo_hz": "within 150 Hz",
    "snr_db": "within 2 dB",
    "frames": "every listed frame decoded with a good CRC (or, where 'crc' is false, no CRC), no other frame reported, no CRC error counted"
  },
